From: Saphira Egg <egg@saphira>
Subject: [PATCH] honour the split-/run layout for the daemon runtime dir

Upstream hardcodes avahi_runtime_dir="/run" (configure.ac:1007), so
the client-request socket compiles to /run/avahi-daemon/socket and
`make install` ships an empty top-level /run directory. On Saphira
/run is a tmpfs that never carries daemon state: ordinary daemon
state lives under /var/run/<service>/ (persistent by design), and
nothing creates /run/avahi-daemon at runtime, so the daemon could
never bind its socket there.

Point the runtime dir at /var/run (consistent with
--localstatedir=/var and the fhs.d/avahi convergence). The socket
macro, the install mkdir, and the pid-adjacent paths all derive from
this one variable, so they move together.

Deliberately patched against the generated `configure` script, not
configure.ac: regenerating would drag the autotools chain into the
closure for a one-line substitution, and no other patch touches
autotools inputs (no autoreconf anywhere in this recipe).
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -24638,7 +24638,7 @@
 #
 # Avahi runtime dir
 #
-avahi_runtime_dir="/run"
+avahi_runtime_dir="/var/run"
 avahi_socket="${avahi_runtime_dir}/avahi-daemon/socket"


